>In article <1990Jan19.174757.5737@anet.ann-arbor.mi.us> wizard@anet.ann-arbor.mi.us (Matt Royle) writes:
>> Why dont you just do polymorph like old Hack does it?
>>Where you can only polymorph the top item on a pile, that way, about
>>the most you can do at one time is 5, by lining them up....
>> Would prevent misuse of polymorph, without changing anything else.

As I understand it, the main problem with polymorphing is getting
infinite wishes. I suggest that it be impossible to get any wish
item through polymorph. This would still allow for having fun
searching through piles, but would eliminate the synergistic effect
of wishes and polymorph. 
I would also like to suggest an e-mail survey by the development
team as to how to best adapt/change this interesting bug/feature.

